{"tool_name":"baldr","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"baldr","home":"https://www.bosingerlab.com/baldr/","license":"MIT","summary":"Pipeline for reconstructing human or rhesus macaque immunoglobulin(Ig)/B cell receptor(BCR) sequences from single cell RNA-Seq data generated by Illumina sequencing","addition_date":"2018-11-13T15:10:31Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:59:01Z","tool_type":["Workflow"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:baldr","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://www.bosingerlab.com/contact/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/BosingerLab/BALDR"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"RNA sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3495"},"format":[{"term":"FASTQ-like format (text)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2182"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"De-novo assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0524"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2082"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"BALDR","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13073-018-0528-3","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2018 The Author(s).B cells play a critical role in the immune response by producing antibodies, which display remarkable diversity. Here we describe a bioinformatic pipeline, BALDR (BCR Assignment of Lineage using De novo Reconstruction) that accurately reconstructs the paired heavy and light chain immunoglobulin gene sequences from Illumina single-cell RNA-seq data. BALDR was accurate for clonotype identification in human and rhesus macaque influenza vaccine and simian immunodeficiency virus vaccine induced vaccine-induced plasmablasts and na\u00efve and antigen-specific memory B cells. BALDR enables matching of clonotype